== TC303_field_on_string
a.hx:2:10: error TC303: name is string, which has no fields
  |
2 | <p>{name.length}</p>
  |          ^^^^^^
  = fix: only structs, forms and form fields have fields

== TC304_unknown_type
a.hx:1:15: error TC304: unknown type Task
  |
1 | component A(t Task)
  |               ^^^^
  = fix: types are string, int, float, bool, slot, or a struct declared in a .go file next to the template (package app)

== TC304_go_float
a.hx:1:19: error TC304: unknown type float64
  |
1 | component A(price float64)
  |                   ^^^^^^^
  = fix: template floats are written float

== TC304_slot_list
a.hx:1:19: error TC304: a list of slots isn't supported
  |
1 | component A(items []slot)
  |                   ^^^^^^
  = fix: declare a single slot parameter

== TC305_string_plus_int
a.hx:2:5: error TC305: + can't be applied to string and int
  |
2 | <p>{name + n}</p>
  |     ^^^^^^^^
  = fix: + adds two ints or two floats, or joins two strings; both sides must have the same type

== TC305_and_on_list
a.hx:2:9: error TC305: && can't be applied to []Todo and bool
  |
2 | <p :if={todos && ok}>x</p>
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: && needs bools on both sides; compare explicitly, e.g. len(x) > 0

== TC305_not_on_string
a.hx:2:9: error TC305: ! can't be applied to name (string)
  |
2 | <p :if={!name}>x</p>
  |         ^^^^^
  = fix: ! needs a bool; - needs an int or float

== TC306_if_not_bool
a.hx:2:9: error TC306: :if needs a bool, but todos is []Todo
  |
2 | <p :if={todos}>none</p>
  |         ^^^^^
  = fix: templates don't treat values as true or false; compare explicitly, e.g. len(todos) > 0

== TC306_inline_if_cond
a.hx:2:8: error TC306: inline if needs a bool, but n is int
  |
2 | <p>{if n, "some", "none"}</p>
  |        ^
  = fix: templates don't treat values as true or false; compare explicitly, e.g. n > 0

== TC307_branches_differ
a.hx:2:5: error TC307: inline if branches have different types: string and int
  |
2 | <p>{if done, "yes", 0}</p>
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: make both branches the same type

== TC308_index_string
a.hx:2:5: error TC308: name is string, which can't be indexed
  |
2 | <p>{name[0]}</p>
  |     ^^^^^^^
  = fix: only lists can be indexed, e.g. items[0]

== TC308_index_not_int
a.hx:2:11: error TC308: list index must be an int, but "a" is string
  |
2 | <p>{todos["a"].title}</p>
  |           ^^^
  = fix: index with an int, e.g. items[0]

== TC309_for_over_struct
a.hx:2:16: error TC309: :for needs a list, but user is User
  |
2 | <li :for={t <- user}>{t.title}</li>
  |                ^^^^
  = fix: loop over a list, e.g. :for={item <- items} where items is a []T parameter or field

== TC310_unknown_helper
a.hx:2:5: error TC310: unknown helper strings_to_upper
  |
2 | <p>{strings_to_upper(name)}</p>
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: templates can't call Go functions directly; declare a pure Go function StringsToUpper in this package with a //loom:helper comment, or compute the value in Go and pass it in

== TC310_helper_typo
a.hx:2:5: error TC310: unknown helper uper
  |
2 | <p>{uper(name)}</p>
  |     ^^^^
  = fix: did you mean upper?

