== TC349_unknown_hint
a.hx:2:39: error TC349: unknown hint optimistic:disable
  |
2 | <button on:click="delete" val-id={id} optimistic:disable>Delete</button>
  |                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: did you mean optimistic:disabled? The hints are optimistic:class, optimistic:disabled and optimistic:hidden

== TC349_unknown_hint_no_suggestion
a.hx:2:27: error TC349: unknown hint optimistic:spin
  |
2 | <button on:click="delete" optimistic:spin>Delete</button>
  |                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: the hints are optimistic:class="names", optimistic:disabled and optimistic:hidden

== TC350_class_expression
a.hx:2:43: error TC350: optimistic:class takes class names as a quoted string
  |
2 | <input type="checkbox" on:change="toggle" optimistic:class={if done, "", "done"} />
  |                                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: write e.g. optimistic:class="done"; hints are static, so the server's render, not an expression, decides what shows once the event is handled

== TC350_class_bare
a.hx:2:43: error TC350: optimistic:class takes class names as a quoted string
  |
2 | <input type="checkbox" on:change="toggle" optimistic:class />
  |                                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: write e.g. optimistic:class="done"; hints are static, so the server's render, not an expression, decides what shows once the event is handled

== TC350_disabled_value
a.hx:2:25: error TC350: optimistic:disabled takes no value
  |
2 | <button on:click="save" optimistic:disabled="true">Save</button>
  |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: write optimistic:disabled alone; it applies while the event is pending

== TC351_hint_without_event
a.hx:2:5: error TC351: optimistic:hidden is on a tag with no on:* event, so it never applies
  |
2 | <li optimistic:hidden>x</li>
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: put it on the element or component call whose on:* event it anticipates, e.g. <button on:click="delete" optimistic:hidden>

== TC351_hint_on_call_without_event
a.hx:2:19: error TC351: optimistic:hidden is on a tag with no on:* event, so it never applies
  |
2 | <.badge label="x" optimistic:hidden />
  |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: put it on the element or component call whose on:* event it anticipates, e.g. <button on:click="delete" optimistic:hidden>

== TC341_joined_class
a.hx:2:16: error TC341: class names are listed, not joined with +
  |
2 | <button class={"btn-" + size}>x</button>
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: list each class as a value, e.g. class={"btn" size}, and style the combination (.btn.sm) in the component's <style>

== TC342_unknown_import
a.hx:1:8: error TC342: can't find a template package at "example.com/app/missing"
  |
1 | import "example.com/app/missing"
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: import a directory of .hx files in this module by its full import path: the module path from go.mod, then the directory; loom components add creates components/

== TC342_unused_import
a.hx:1:8: error TC342: "example.com/app/components" is imported but none of its components or behaviors is used
  |
1 | import "example.com/app/components"
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: remove the import

== TC342_import_clash
a.hx:1:8: error TC342: "example.com/app/components" exports component Button, which this package also declares
  |
1 | import "example.com/app/components"
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: rename the local component Button; calls aren't qualified, so each name must mean one component

== TC343_no_module
a.hx:1:10: error TC343: behavior menu has no module: menu.js doesn't exist
  |
1 | behavior menu(open bool)
  |          ^^^^
  = fix: write menu.js next to a.hx, exporting function mount(el, props, emit) that returns {update, destroy}

== TC343_no_mount
a.hx:1:10: error TC343: menu.js doesn't export mount
  |
1 | behavior menu(open bool)
  |          ^^^^
  = fix: add export function mount(el, props, emit) { ...; return {update(props) {...}, destroy() {...}} }

== TC343_prop_type
a.hx:1:20: error TC343: todo is Todo, which a behavior can't take
  |
1 | behavior menu(todo Todo)
  |                    ^^^^
  = fix: props are sent to the browser as JSON: use string, int, float, bool, an enum, or a list of those

== TC344_unknown_behavior
a.hx:3:5: error TC344: unknown behavior mneu
  |
3 | <ul use:mneu={open: true}></ul>
  |     ^^^^^^^^
  = fix: did you mean use:menu?

== TC344_unknown_prop
a.hx:3:15: error TC344: behavior menu has no prop opn
  |
3 | <ul use:menu={opn: true}></ul>
  |               ^^^
  = fix: did you mean open? Its props are: open

== TC344_missing_prop
a.hx:3:5: error TC344: use:menu is missing open
  |
3 | <ul use:menu></ul>
  |     ^^^^^^^^
  = fix: pass every prop without a default: use:menu={open: ...}

== TC344_prop_wrong_type
a.hx:3:21: error TC344: prop open is bool, but n is int
  |
3 | <ul use:menu={open: n}></ul>
  |                     ^
  = fix: pass a value of type bool

== TC345_requires_missing
a.hx:3:5: error TC345: use:menu requires [role="listbox"], but <ul> has no role
  |
3 | <ul use:menu></ul>
  |     ^^^^^^^^
  = fix: add role="listbox" to the <ul>

== TC345_requires_value
a.hx:3:5: error TC345: use:menu requires [role="listbox"], but this is role="menu"
  |
3 | <ul role="menu" use:menu></ul>
  |     ^^^^
  = fix: write role="listbox", or use another behavior

== TC346_not_emitted
a.hx:3:14: error TC346: on:select isn't an event this element sends
  |
3 | <ul use:menu on:select="pick"></ul>
  |              ^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: the DOM events are click, change, input, submit, keydown, keyup, focus and blur; behavior menu emits close

== TC346_no_behavior
a.hx:2:6: error TC346: on:mouseover isn't an event this element sends
  |
2 | <div on:mouseover="hover"></div>
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: the DOM events are click, change, input, submit, keydown, keyup, focus and blur; other events come from a behavior, declared with emits (mouseover) and attached with use:

== ST701_tokens_syntax
tokens.toml:2:10: error ST701: the value of accent must be a quoted string
  |
2 | accent = #4f46e5
  |          ^
  = fix: write accent = "value", or { light = "...", dark = "..." } for a color with a dark value
a.hx:2:19: error ST703: unknown token color.accent
  |
2 | <style>p { color: token(color.accent) }</style>
  |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: tokens.toml has no color tokens yet; add accent to its [color] group

== ST701_token_outside_group
tokens.toml:1:1: error ST701: token accent is not in a group
  |
1 | accent = "#4f46e5"
  | ^^^^^^
  = fix: put a group header such as [color] or [space] above it

== ST702_token_not_a_color
tokens.toml:2:1: error ST702: color.accent is "blueish", which is not a color
  |
2 | accent = "blueish"
  | ^^^^^^
  = fix: write a color as #rrggbb, rgb(...), hsl(...) or oklch(...), e.g. "#4f46e5"
tokens.toml:4:1: error ST702: space.2 has a dark value, but only colors and shadows can
  |
4 | 2 = { light = "0.5rem", dark = "1rem" }
  | ^
  = fix: give space.2 one value

== ST703_unknown_token
a.hx:2:19: error ST703: unknown token color.acent
  |
2 | <style>p { color: token(color.acent); padding: token(space.3) }</style>
  |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: did you mean token(color.accent)?
a.hx:2:48: error ST703: unknown token space.3
  |
2 | <style>p { color: token(color.acent); padding: token(space.3) }</style>
  |                                                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: the space tokens are token(space.1) (0.25rem), token(space.2) (0.5rem), token(space.4) (1rem); add space.3 to tokens.toml if it's missing

== ST703_no_tokens_file
a.hx:2:19: error ST703: token(color.accent) is used, but there is no tokens.toml
  |
2 | <style>p { color: token(color.accent) }</style>
  |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: create tokens.toml in the app (next to go.mod, or in this directory or a parent) with a [color] group defining accent

== ST704_raw_values
a.hx:3:23: error ST704: raw color #fff in background
  |
3 |   .card { background: #fff; padding: 12px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 14px; box-shadow: 0 2px 4px black; }
  |                       ^^^^
  = fix: use a color token: token(color.on-accent) (#ffffff), token(color.surface) (#ffffff), token(color.accent) (#4f46e5); or add one to tokens.toml
a.hx:3:38: error ST704: raw spacing 12px in padding
  |
3 |   .card { background: #fff; padding: 12px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 14px; box-shadow: 0 2px 4px black; }
  |                                      ^^^^
  = fix: use a space token: token(space.2) (0.5rem), token(space.4) (1rem), token(space.1) (0.25rem); or add one to tokens.toml
a.hx:3:59: error ST704: raw radius 5px in border-radius
  |
3 |   .card { background: #fff; padding: 12px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 14px; box-shadow: 0 2px 4px black; }
  |                                                           ^^^
  = fix: use a radius token: token(radius.md) (6px); or add one to tokens.toml
a.hx:3:75: error ST704: raw font size 14px in font-size
  |
3 |   .card { background: #fff; padding: 12px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 14px; box-shadow: 0 2px 4px black; }
  |                                                                           ^^^^
  = fix: use a text token: token(text.sm) (0.875rem), token(text.md) (1rem); or add one to tokens.toml
a.hx:3:93: error ST704: raw shadow 0 2px 4px black in box-shadow
  |
3 |   .card { background: #fff; padding: 12px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 14px; box-shadow: 0 2px 4px black; }
  |                                                                                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: use a shadow token: token(shadow.card) (0 1px 3px #0003); or add one to tokens.toml
a.hx:4:20: error ST704: var(--color-accent) refers to a token directly
  |
4 |   .card a { color: var(--color-accent); border: 1px solid red; width: 50%; margin: 0 auto; }
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: write token(color.accent), so the compiler can check it
a.hx:4:59: error ST704: raw color red in border
  |
4 |   .card a { color: var(--color-accent); border: 1px solid red; width: 50%; margin: 0 auto; }
  |                                                           ^^^
  = fix: use a color token: token(color.text) (#18181b), token(color.accent) (#4f46e5), token(color.on-accent) (#ffffff); or add one to tokens.toml

== ST705_unsafe_style
a.hx:2:1: warning ST705: unsafe style block in A: raw values aren't checked
  |
2 | <style unsafe>p { color: #b83f45; padding: 3px }</style>
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: replace raw colors, spacing, radii, font sizes and shadows with token(...) and remove unsafe

== ST706_low_contrast
tokens.toml:3:1: warning ST706: color.on-accent on color.accent has contrast 1.49:1 in dark mode, below the 4.5:1 WCAG AA needs for text
  |
3 | on-accent = "#ffffff"
  | ^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: make color.on-accent or color.accent lighter or darker until the ratio is at least 4.5:1

== ST706_low_contrast_in_theme
tokens.toml:5:1: warning ST706: color.on-accent on color.accent has contrast 1.23:1 in light mode in theme pale, below the 4.5:1 WCAG AA needs for text
  |
5 | accent = "#e0e7ff"
  | ^^^^^^
  = fix: make color.on-accent or color.accent lighter or darker until the ratio is at least 4.5:1

== ST711_theme_unknown_token
tokens.toml:4:1: error ST711: theme amiga overrides color.acent, which isn't a token
  |
4 | acent = "#ff8800"
  | ^^^^^
  = fix: did you mean accent? a theme overrides tokens declared outside it
tokens.toml:5:2: error ST711: theme amiga overrides group [space], which has no tokens
  |
5 | [theme.amiga.space]
  |  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: a theme overrides tokens declared outside it; declare the group's tokens first, or use one of: color

== ST711_theme_bad_name
tokens.toml:3:2: error ST711: invalid theme name "dark"
  |
3 | [theme.dark.color]
  |  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: name a theme with lower-case letters, digits and '-', other than light and dark (the modes), e.g. [theme.amiga.color]

== ST712_unknown_theme
a.hx:2:6: error ST712: data-theme="amgia" names no theme
  |
2 | <div data-theme="amgia"><p data-theme="dark">x</p></div>
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: did you mean "amiga"? the themes are light, dark, amiga

== ST712_theme_not_written_out
a.hx:2:18: error ST712: data-theme takes theme names written out, but platform could be any string
  |
2 | <div data-theme={platform}><p data-theme={if platform == "c64", "c64", "amiga"}>x</p></div>
  |                  ^^^^^^^^
  = fix: choose between names with an inline if, e.g. data-theme={if t.platform == "amiga", "amiga", ""}, so each one is checked
a.hx:2:65: error ST712: data-theme="c64" names no theme
  |
2 | <div data-theme={platform}><p data-theme={if platform == "c64", "c64", "amiga"}>x</p></div>
  |                                                                 ^^^^^
  = fix: use one of light, dark, amiga, or declare it in tokens.toml under [theme.c64.color]

== ST707_style_nested
a.hx:2:6: error ST707: <style> must be at the top level of component A
  |
2 | <div><style>p { color: token(color.text) }</style></div>
  |      ^^^^^^
  = fix: move it to the top level of the component, outside any element; its CSS is scoped to the component and linked by <.loom_styles /> in the root layout

== ST707_style_attributes
a.hx:2:8: error ST707: <style> takes no attribute scoped
  |
2 | <style scoped :if={true}>p { color: token(color.text) }</style>
  |        ^^^^^^
  = fix: the only attribute is unsafe, which allows raw values: <style unsafe>
a.hx:2:1: error ST707: <style> can't take :for or :if
  |
2 | <style scoped :if={true}>p { color: token(color.text) }</style>
  | ^^^^^^
  = fix: a style block is static; style a state with a class, e.g. class={if done, "done", ""}
a.hx:3:1: error ST707: component A has more than one <style> block
  |
3 | <style>a { color: token(color.text) }</style>
  | ^^^^^^
  = fix: merge them into one <style> block; the first is at line 2

== ST708_css_syntax
a.hx:2:37: error ST708: a rule is never closed
  |
2 | <style>p { color: token(color.text) </style>
  |                                     ^
  = fix: add the missing '}'

== ST708_nested_rule
a.hx:2:42: error ST708: nested rules aren't supported
  |
2 | <style>.card { color: token(color.text); a { color: token(color.accent) } }</style>
  |                                          ^^^
  = fix: move the rule out to the top level of the style block, with its full selector

== ST708_import
a.hx:2:8: error ST708: @import isn't supported in a component's style
  |
2 | <style>@import "base.css";</style>
  |        ^^^^^^^
  = fix: styles are per component; put shared styles in the component that renders the elements, or in the root layout

== ST709_global_outside_root
a.hx:2:8: error ST709: :global(...) can only be used in a root layout
  |
2 | <style>:global(body) p { color: token(color.text) }</style>
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: style elements from the component that renders them; global styles for the document go in the root layout

== ST710_wrong_token_group
a.hx:2:21: error ST710: padding takes space tokens, not color.accent
  |
2 | <style>p { padding: token(color.accent); color: token(space.2) }</style>
  |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: use a space token, e.g. token(space.1)
a.hx:2:49: error ST710: color takes color tokens, not space.2
  |
2 | <style>p { padding: token(color.accent); color: token(space.2) }</style>
  |                                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: use a color token, e.g. token(color.accent)

== TC347_preview_enum
a.hx:1:44: error TC347: size is :sm | :md, so previews already show each of its values
  |
1 | component A(size: :sm | :md = :sm @preview("sm"))
  |                                            ^
  = fix: remove @preview from size

== TC347_preview_bool
a.hx:1:32: error TC347: busy is bool, so previews already show each of its values
  |
1 | component A(busy bool @preview(true))
  |                                ^
  = fix: remove @preview from busy

== TC347_preview_list
a.hx:1:37: error TC347: items is []string, which @preview can't give a value
  |
1 | component A(items []string @preview("a"))
  |                                     ^
  = fix: @preview takes strings, numbers and slot text; to preview a component that needs []string, wrap it in one that builds the value

== TC347_preview_type
a.hx:1:28: error TC347: the @preview values of n must be int literals
  |
1 | component A(n int @preview("one"), inner_block slot @preview(1))
  |                            ^^^^^
  = fix: write values like @preview(1, 20)
a.hx:1:62: error TC347: the @preview values of inner_block must be markup (string) literals
  |
1 | component A(n int @preview("one"), inner_block slot @preview(1))
  |                                                              ^
  = fix: write values like @preview("<p>Some content</p>")

== TC348_for_without_key
a.hx:2:15: warning TC348: :for over Todo has no :key, so items are matched by position
  |
2 | <ul><li :for={t <- todos}>{t.title}<em :for={tag <- tags}>{tag}</em></li></ul>
  |               ^
  = fix: add :key={t.id}

== TC353_inline_script
a.hx:2:6: warning TC353: this inline <script> won't run: the Content-Security-Policy blocks inline script
  |
2 | <div><script>alert(1)</script><script type="application/json">{}</script><script src="/app.js"></script></div>
  |      ^^^^^^^
  = fix: move the code to a file the app serves and load it with <script src=...>, or write a behavior (use:name), see docs/components.md

== TC353_inline_handler
a.hx:2:9: warning TC353: the inline handler onclick won't run: the Content-Security-Policy blocks inline script
  |
2 | <button onclick="go()">Go</button>
  |         ^^^^^^^
  = fix: bind the event with on:click="name" and handle it in Go, or attach the code with a behavior (use:name), see docs/components.md

== TC352_form_field_type
a.hx:1:15: error TC352: field Signup.Born has Go type time.Time, which a form can't decode
  |
1 | component A(f form[Signup])
  |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: form fields are string, int, int64, float64, bool, map[string]string or map[string]bool; use a string and parse it in Validate

== TC302_form_field
a.hx:2:16: error TC302: form Signup has no field nmae
  |
2 | <input name={f.nmae.name} value={f.Name.value} />
  |                ^^^^
  = fix: did you mean name? the form's fields are Signup's exported fields: name, shares
a.hx:2:36: error TC302: form Signup has no field Name
  |
2 | <input name={f.nmae.name} value={f.Name.value} />
  |                                    ^^^^
  = fix: template field names are snake_case: write f.name

== TC304_form_input
a.hx:1:15: error TC304: unknown type Singup in form[Singup]
  |
1 | component A(f form[Singup], g form, h string[Signup])
  |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: did you mean form[Signup]?
a.hx:1:31: error TC304: form needs the struct it decodes to, in brackets
  |
1 | component A(f form[Singup], g form, h string[Signup])
  |                               ^^^^
  = fix: write form[SettleInput], naming a struct declared in a .go file next to the template
a.hx:1:39: error TC304: string takes no type argument
  |
1 | component A(f form[Singup], g form, h string[Signup])
  |                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: only form takes one, as in form[SettleInput]

== TC314_form_field_attribute
a.hx:2:14: error TC314: attribute name can't take a field
  |
2 | <input name={f.name} />
  |              ^^^^^^
  = fix: write name={f.name.name}, or pass the field to a kit input: <.input field={f.name} />
a.hx:3:5: error TC313: f.shares is a map field and can't be rendered as text
  |
3 | <p>{f.shares}</p>
  |     ^^^^^^^^
  = fix: index the map field with a key: f.shares[key]

== TC303_form_entries
a.hx:2:23: error TC303: f.shares is a map field, which has an entry per key, not fields
  |
2 | <input name={f.shares.sam} value={f.shares[1].value} />
  |                       ^^^
  = fix: index it with a key: f.shares[sam]
a.hx:2:44: error TC308: a map field's key must be a string, but 1 is int
  |
2 | <input name={f.shares.sam} value={f.shares[1].value} />
  |                                            ^
  = fix: index with a string, e.g. f.shares[person.id]

